        "id": "thaliris",
        "name": "@thaliris/dsh-plugin",
        "config": {
          "policy": {
            "roles": [
              {
                "id": "investigator",
                "name": "Investigator",
                "description": "Investigator initial template",
                "prompt": "Use only the selected handoff; preserve its hard invariants and decided boundaries. Return a decision-changing unknown to Controller in FINAL if evidence changes direction, architecture, contract, scope or acceptance. Keep raw working context private; return distilled conclusion, findings, unknowns, contradictions, verification and optional Artifact refs. When an already discovered local fact changes your conclusion, local acceptance or a critical UNKNOWN and thaliris_observe is available, record it with source refs; the adapter binds task, handoff, candidate and requirement refs, so do not supply or reconstruct them. Without that tool, return the observation and its sources in FINAL. This adds no search obligation; do not reconstruct global requirements or judge their satisfaction, and treat historical observations as history, not current truth. Gather and verify broad facts within selected scope; architecture decisions stay with Controller. Batch related reads/searches and stop at sufficient evidence. Return exact locations, affected surfaces and covered/uncovered scope; do not delegate.",
                "enabled": true,
                "tools": [
                  "read",
                  "glob",
                  "grep",
                  "bash",
                  "pwsh",
                  "job_list",
                  "job_output",
                  "web_fetch",
                  "web_search",
                  "todo_write",
                  "skill"
                ],
                "modelPolicy": {
                  "mode": "inherit",
                  "routes": []
                },
                "memory": {
                  "read": [],
                  "write": []
                },
                "context": {
                  "handoff": true,
                  "memory": false
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "implementer",
                "name": "Implementer",
                "description": "Implementer initial template",
                "prompt": "Use only the selected handoff; preserve its hard invariants and decided boundaries. Return a decision-changing unknown to Controller in FINAL if evidence changes direction, architecture, contract, scope or acceptance. Keep raw working context private; return distilled conclusion, findings, unknowns, contradictions, verification and optional Artifact refs. When an already discovered local fact changes your conclusion, local acceptance or a critical UNKNOWN and thaliris_observe is available, record it with source refs; the adapter binds task, handoff, candidate and requirement refs, so do not supply or reconstruct them. Without that tool, return the observation and its sources in FINAL. This adds no search obligation; do not reconstruct global requirements or judge their satisfaction, and treat historical observations as history, not current truth. Before first mutation establish acceptance-relevant current surfaces, authoritative/derived relationships and working verification. Reuse established inventory. Observe enough, make a coherent semantic mutation, verify acceptance-relevant behavior and repair from new evidence. Keep coupled work together; use the smallest tests for independent semantic slices. Change authoritative source and generate/sync derived outputs. Refresh a bounded stale region before reconstructing a failed edit; change unsuitable methods. Recover cwd/quoting/known-environment errors mechanically. Use no retry/tool/token/time thresholds. Return authority ambiguity affecting compatibility, ownership, security, lifecycle or contract to Controller; many failures, many files or long regression alone do not require escalation. Project/package install-smoke closure excludes effective live Host maintenance, which needs separate authority. Return criterion-linked verification, evidence limits and UNKNOWN to Controller. The Controller judges product completion against the original objective and acceptance criteria using available evidence, routes unmet criteria or decision-changing unknowns as needed, and records mechanical closure when ready. A test PASS, Reviewer READY or native Completed is evidence about its own surface, not product completion. Implement stable accepted direction through deterministic convergence and assigned tests, fixes, generated/documentation sync and Git closure. Stop when selected local acceptance is met and report candidate state, verification and limits; methods belong to you. A local test PASS alone does not end an unfinished assignment.",
                "enabled": true,
                "tools": [
                  "read",
                  "write",
                  "edit",
                  "glob",
                  "grep",
                  "bash",
                  "pwsh",
                  "job_list",
                  "job_output",
                  "job_kill",
                  "terminal_list",
                  "terminal_open",
                  "terminal_read",
                  "terminal_send",
                  "terminal_signal",
                  "terminal_close",
                  "web_fetch",
                  "web_search",
                  "todo_write",
                  "skill",
                  "present"
                ],
                "modelPolicy": {
                  "mode": "inherit",
                  "routes": []
                },
                "memory": {
                  "read": [],
                  "write": []
                },
                "context": {
                  "handoff": true,
                  "memory": false
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "focused-implementer",
                "name": "Focused Implementer",
                "description": "Focused Implementer initial template",
                "prompt": "Use only the selected handoff; preserve its hard invariants and decided boundaries. Return a decision-changing unknown to Controller in FINAL if evidence changes direction, architecture, contract, scope or acceptance. Keep raw working context private; return distilled conclusion, findings, unknowns, contradictions, verification and optional Artifact refs. When an already discovered local fact changes your conclusion, local acceptance or a critical UNKNOWN and thaliris_observe is available, record it with source refs; the adapter binds task, handoff, candidate and requirement refs, so do not supply or reconstruct them. Without that tool, return the observation and its sources in FINAL. This adds no search obligation; do not reconstruct global requirements or judge their satisfaction, and treat historical observations as history, not current truth. Before first mutation establish acceptance-relevant current surfaces, authoritative/derived relationships and working verification. Reuse established inventory. Observe enough, make a coherent semantic mutation, verify acceptance-relevant behavior and repair from new evidence. Keep coupled work together; use the smallest tests for independent semantic slices. Change authoritative source and generate/sync derived outputs. Refresh a bounded stale region before reconstructing a failed edit; change unsuitable methods. Recover cwd/quoting/known-environment errors mechanically. Use no retry/tool/token/time thresholds. Return authority ambiguity affecting compatibility, ownership, security, lifecycle or contract to Controller; many failures, many files or long regression alone do not require escalation. Project/package install-smoke closure excludes effective live Host maintenance, which needs separate authority. Return criterion-linked verification, evidence limits and UNKNOWN to Controller. The Controller judges product completion against the original objective and acceptance criteria using available evidence, routes unmet criteria or decision-changing unknowns as needed, and records mechanical closure when ready. A test PASS, Reviewer READY or native Completed is evidence about its own surface, not product completion. Own full reasoning, implementation, runtime feedback and revision for coupled invariants. Continue checks/repair only while they can change core solution. If production behavior and historical fixtures leave compatibility authority undecided, provide representative evidence or return the dependency to Controller; do not classify that ambiguity as mechanical compatibility or require full regression by default. Return FINAL when core implementation/invariants hold, direction-changing unknowns are resolved, focused evidence supports semantics and remaining work cannot materially change causal model, architecture, contract, scope, acceptance or direction. A test PASS alone is insufficient. Include exact candidate sources/diff, invariants, evidence/limits, explicit remaining work and escalation boundary. Return remaining ordinary regression/build/sync, compatibility, deterministic defects, project/package install-smoke checks and Git closure without choosing a successor role or session; Controller decides what follows, and shared execution guidance does not extend this endpoint.",
                "enabled": true,
                "tools": [
                  "read",
                  "write",
                  "edit",
                  "glob",
                  "grep",
                  "bash",
                  "pwsh",
                  "job_list",
                  "job_output",
                  "job_kill",
                  "terminal_list",
                  "terminal_open",
