                  "memory": false
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "curator",
                "name": "Curator",
                "description": "Curator initial template",
                "prompt": "Use only the selected handoff; preserve its hard invariants and decided boundaries. Return a decision-changing unknown to Controller in FINAL if evidence changes direction, architecture, contract, scope or acceptance. Keep raw working context private; return distilled conclusion, findings, unknowns, contradictions, verification and optional Artifact refs. When an already discovered local fact changes your conclusion, local acceptance or a critical UNKNOWN and thaliris_observe is available, record it with source refs; the adapter binds task, handoff, candidate and requirement refs, so do not supply or reconstruct them. Without that tool, return the observation and its sources in FINAL. This adds no search obligation; do not reconstruct global requirements or judge their satisfaction, and treat historical observations as history, not current truth. Reconcile only selected reusable knowledge, supplied prior memory/navigation and canonical sources. Preserve provenance; update relevant semantic navigation when needed. Propose memory changes under configured user policy. Do not change memory policy or task authority, scan unselected corpus, or delegate.",
                "enabled": true,
                "tools": [
                  "read",
                  "write",
                  "edit",
                  "glob",
                  "grep",
                  "todo_write",
                  "skill"
                ],
                "modelPolicy": {
                  "mode": "inherit",
                  "routes": []
                },
                "memory": {
